# tools/witness.list — DECLARED WITNESS QUOTATIONS (citecheck's second class)
#
# WHAT: a reference that a document is TALKING ABOUT — a quotation of a citation
# (a drift report, a rule's worked example, a decision-log entry describing the
# very ref it quotes) — rather than a live pointer an agent is expected to follow.
#
# WHY DECLARED INSTEAD OF EDITED IN: the surfaces that carry these quotations are
# append-only records or pinned doctrine (INTEGRITY.md is a pin file; LOG.md and
# CONTEXT.md are append-only by rule), so the quotation cannot be rewritten in place.
# Declaring it is the lawful move — and the tool CHECKS this list every run: an
# entry whose line no longer carries the ref is reported as register rot, never
# auto-dropped (R14: no silent fixes; a hand-maintained index must be verified too).
#
# FORMAT: one entry per line —  <file>:<srcline>  <ref>  —  <why it is a witness>
#   (leading '#' and blank lines are ignored)
#
# THE CONVENTION (why these exist at all): a live citation is written in plain
# prose; a quotation of a citation is written in backticks or a code fence. The
# tool strips those before matching. These four entries were written as PLAIN
# PROSE by the 2026-09-19 adoption moment — the tool's own rule was not applied
# to the tool's own authors, so the gate cried wolf on 4 of 14 findings
# (research/ergonomics-39d-audit.md §3-F-2). Declaring them restores the gate's
# signal; the deeper fix (a witness-marking convention in doctrine) is staged in
# proposals/pr-025.
#
./CONTEXT.md:704 AGENTS.md:74-77 — the 2026-09-11 ergonomics-deep entry quotes the drift it found (a description of a citation, not a pointer to it)
./CONTEXT.md:706 VERSION.md:26-27 — the 2026-09-19 adoption entry quotes the drift the sweep caught in that moment
./CONTEXT.md:706 AGENTS.md:74-77 — the 2026-09-19 adoption entry quotes the same drift it re-anchored
./INTEGRITY.md:55 AGENTS.md:74-77 — the citecheck Rule's worked example (the live case the rule was written for)
./LOG.md:324 AGENTS.md:74-77 — the LOG entry for the 2026-09-19 moment, quoting the same worked example
